{:edb/db-before-t 13829 :edb/db-after-t 13830 :edb/tx-data [[13194139547142 50 #inst "2026-11-10T13:08:35.697Z" 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186707100 1068 #edb/ref 17592186707062 13194139547142 17592186576411 false] [17592186707100 1068 #edb/ref 17592186756028 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186707100 1068 #edb/ref 17592186756031 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186707100 1068 #edb/ref 17592186756034 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186707100 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$.\n\nII. $x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$.\n\nIII. The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1}, \\mathbf{a}_{2}, \\mathbf{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent." 13194139547142 17592186576411 false] [17592186707100 1071 "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad \\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186707100 1074 "A set is **linearly independent** when the equation $x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$. A nontrivial solution proves **linear dependence**.\n\nTest the proposed combination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}&=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\ne\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe homogeneous vector equation gives the coordinate system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1}-2x_{2} &=0 \\\\ -2x_{2}-x_{3} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nChoose one coefficient nonzero and solve the remaining coordinate equations by substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_{2}&=1 \\\\ x_{1}-2(1)&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{1}=2 \\\\ -2(1)-x_{3}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{3}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives a nontrivial solution. Verify it directly:\n\n$$\n2\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nThe coefficients are not all zero, so the set is **linearly dependent**.\n\nA failed candidate alone does not prove independence; the homogeneous-equation argument settles the classification.\n\nStatement I is **false**. Statement II is **false**. Statement III is **false**." 13194139547142 17592186576411 false] [17592186707100 1074 "A set is **linearly independent** when the equation $x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the solution $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$. A nontrivial solution proves **linear dependence**.\n\nTest the proposed combination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}&=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\ne\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe homogeneous vector equation gives the coordinate system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x_{1}-2x_{2} &=0 \\\\ -2x_{2}-x_{3} &=0 \\\\ 0 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nChoose one coefficient nonzero and solve the remaining coordinate equations by substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x_{2}&=1 \\\\ x_{1}-2(1)&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{1}=2 \\\\ -2(1)-x_{3}&=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x_{3}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives a nontrivial solution. Verify it directly:\n\n$$\n2\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}-2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nThe coefficients are not all zero, so the set is **linearly dependent**.\n\nA failed candidate alone does not prove independence; the homogeneous-equation argument settles the classification.\n\nThe statement “$\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$.” is **false**. The statement “$x_{1}\\mathbf{a}_{1}+x_{2}\\mathbf{a}_{2}+x_{3}\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if $x_{1}=x_{2}=x_{3}=0$.” is **false**. The statement “The set $\\{\\mathbf{a}_{1}, \\mathbf{a}_{2}, \\mathbf{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.” is **false**." 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186756028 1075 #edb/ref 17592186756029 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186756028 1075 #edb/ref 17592186756030 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186756028 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186756028 1077 "$\\mathbf{a}_{1}+\\mathbf{a}_{2}+2\\mathbf{a}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$." 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186756028 1078 #edb/ref 17592186756029 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186756028 1079 #uuid "b90baa65-8cd3-5ec1-ac5f-443c3a97ac45" 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186756029 1080 "false" 13194139547142 17592186576411 true] [17592186756029 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139547142 1759218657641